[36m =[0m [36mhelp[0m: [4m:[0m[1;4mfilter-in-statement[0m[4m [0m[4mlocation[0m
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
           Only show the messages logged by the log statement at the given
           source file and line, and those of other filtered-in statements and
           patterns, as found in the source added with :add-source-path.  The
           statement is found again by its function and message each time the
           source is scanned, so the filter follows it when edits move it; if
           its message changes or it is removed, the filter does nothing until
           it is deleted
